WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.183
Week 1: How Spanish Works. spell a name recognize a stressed syllable build a sustainable study loop

2
00:00:07.183 --> 00:00:15.988
Form and meaning. Spanish sound–spelling correspondence, the five stable vowels, syllables, stress, written accents, and punctuation.

3
00:00:15.988 --> 00:00:42.203
Model set. Mi nombre se escribe con cinco letras. La h no tiene sonido. Escucho y repito cada palabra. ¿Cuál es la sílaba tónica? La práctica breve y frecuente funciona mejor. My name is spelled with five letters. The letter h has no sound. I listen to and repeat every word. Which is the stressed syllable? Brief, frequent practice works better.

4
00:00:42.203 --> 00:00:52.333
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:00:52.333 --> 00:01:04.938
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: spell a name; recognize a stressed syllable; build a sustainable study loop. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:04.938 --> 00:01:31.943
Model language. Mi nombre se escribe con cinco letras. — My name is spelled with five letters. La h no tiene sonido. — The letter h has no sound. Escucho y repito cada palabra. — I listen to and repeat every word. ¿Cuál es la sílaba tónica? — Which is the stressed syllable? La práctica breve y frecuente funciona mejor. — Brief, frequent practice works better.

7
00:01:31.943 --> 00:01:42.097
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
